  "interpretation": "Using locally generated Derm Foundation SavedModel embeddings, the 12-seed probe reaches 0.6859 accuracy and 0.3392 macro recall. The conservative MobileNet checkpoint-policy envelope is positive but smaller than the earlier legacy-cache framing. Against the architecture/resolution-matched BiT-M R101x3 ImageNet control, Derm Foundation remains ahead, but by a narrower margin. The result supports dermatology-specific pretraining helping on SCIN downstream evaluation; it is still not external validation and not a solved tail-label classifier.",
  "tail_support_note": "Across the 12 fair MobileNet folds, clinician_review averaged 4.8 validation images, hyperpigmentation 2.6, and rosacea 7.1. Treat per-class tail recall as underpowered diagnostic evidence.",
  "failed_seed_note": "Expanded MobileNet comparison uses matched completed seeds only. Excluded native-Windows MobileNet attempts failed before evaluation for seeds 303, 505, and 606 (3 seeds). Seed 707 also failed natively but was recovered with Docker CPU and is included.",
  "statistical_caveat": "The paired tests compare repeated grouped resamples of the same SCIN case universe. Treat p-values as stability diagnostics over matched seeds, not as independent external-test-set inference.",
